      "side": 0,
      "message": "Right, in WGSL uniform layout 16 is sufficient but std140 would require 32.\n\n\u003e Although, thinking about it some more... if we send matrices in std140 layout, how are we going to read them in WGSL? WGSL thinks a 2x2 matrix is tightly packed.\n\nThis is a very good question as a WGSL `mat2x2\u003cf32\u003e` won\u0027t match a std140 mat2x2.\n\nGiven that we seem to actively write our shaders to use `float4` instead of `mat2x2` just to avoid this problem, and seeing as WGSL emulates something similar under the hood, one solution could be for SkSL to define its matrix types to have tight packing. Under the hood it could convert a mat2x2 to float4 (or two float2\u0027s) when targeting GL or Vulkan and the API side could assume that to be the alignment?",
